  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposal would fail the 25 degree rule and would result in an unacceptable loss of daylight in relation to the primary habitable windows at the adjoining first floor flat at Nos 53-59 High Street. Furthermore, the proposal would significantly reduce levels of outlook from the primary  habitable windows at the adjoining flat resulting in intrusive and overbearing appearance and significantly increased sense of enclosure. As such, the proposal is therefore contrary to policy D3 of the London Plan 2021 and policy DM10 of the LDF Core Strategy 2012.\r",
    "Insufficient information has been submitted regarding the proposed use, proposed operating hours, types and number of the deliveries to demonstrate that the proposal would not lead to an unacceptable rise in noise levels and disturbances in relation to the neighbouring residential properties or would not adversely affect shared access to the flats at No 29 Sussex Place As such, the proposal is therefore contrary to policy D3 of the London Plan 2021 and policy DM10 of the LDF Core Strategy 2012."
  ],
